<title>GERMANY: East German August adjusted unemployment falls.</title>
<headline>East German August adjusted unemployment falls.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Aug 96	 Jul 96	   Aug 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.123 million    1.147 million	1.035</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.133 million    1.145 million	1.033</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     -12,000	-10,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		15.0 pct     15.4 pct	 13.9 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	47,501	 45,633	   55,713</p>
<p> Vacancies		   57,524	 57,253	   53,688</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Jun 96	 May 96</p>
<p>				 +4,000	+12,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49-228-609750</p>
</text>
